    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing... i don't want to \"keep climbing.\" i'm just so exhausted. i've done everything i was supposed to do, i ticked every single box, and i'm still this empty. it's like i've finished the book and there are no more chapters left to write. everything just feels so finalized and permanent. if reaching the summit doesn't change anything, why does the struggle even matter anymore? it feels like the only logical thing left is just... to stop.",
